16.165.m:
Because a curse was pronounced upon you here in the assembly by Sāvitrī,
whatever is given and offered into fire here shall become imperishable;
therefore has this boon been granted to you by me, O best of the twice-born.

‘You are a kinsman, without a doubt; I cannot live without you.
When you are seen, my gaze becomes bright and cheerful;
my mind is exceedingly delighted’—I tell you this in absolute truth.
